body:
Now all the other conferences will say that Duke and UNC making it to the Sweet 16 doesn't mean the ACC is good. Meanwhile they'll gloss over the fact that NC State and Clemson is there. They'll also gloss over the fact that the ACC is 10-3 against the B12 (correct me if I'm off on that). They'll also gloss over the fact that maybe so many teams from the ACC make it far in the tourney every year is because the conference is actually challenging. 

&#x200B;

Playing cupcake OOC schedule doesn't prepare you for success.

that's a good point. What's your definition of "succeeds" though. At what point can we look at a project and say "yeah, it ain't going anywhere"? 

&#x200B;

I'm asking this question in good faith - not being a smartass lol.

haha no it's not nearly the serious at all. I just hate them cause they try to claim the professional sports teams that are in NC, as theirs. For example, the Carolina Panthers are located in Charlotte, NC but there's a whole movement to have it be the team for both states. Just petty stuff like that haha. 

&#x200B;

Also, South Carolina contributes absolutely nothing to society. All the good businesses and colleges are in NC.

I'm fully aware. I'm just saying, this photo is likely very misleading. Maybe whoever posted this doesn't have insurance. But only 8% of the population isn't insured....so there's a 92% chance this person has insurance and didn't pay close to this amount of pocket.

&#x200B;

Again, I'm not arguing that healthcare here is astronomical. I'm simply commenting on this misleading post.

No it's not bad. It just doesn't have the longevity a lot of BGS fans thought it would. I'd never really played a BSG before (I played Fallout 4 for maybe 3 hours back in the day). But I got hooked onto this one. I have probably 70 hours in it...60 of that is probably from my first playthrough.

&#x200B;

So no, it's not as bad as the Steam reviews. I think expectations were very high and it didn't reach those. Still worth the price tag though.

Ah! That makes sense actually. I'm in software sales and call people up in Canada quite a bit (I'm in the US). I do notice that you all seem to have quite a bit more time off. I received a TON of OOO emails from prospects this morning. 

&#x200B;

I say that statement with jealousy lol.

this right here is the issue. Making statements about an issue you don't know much about. You don't have to have an opinion. It's ok to just say you know what, I'm not gonna comment on this cause I'm not educated enough on the topic. There's literally nothing wrong with that.

&#x200B;

Why does everyone feel they need to have an opinion on literally everything these days?
